{
  "id": "main-guard",
  "title": "Program Structure: __main__",
  "exercises": [
    {
      "id": "01",
      "source_unit": "main-guard",
      "title": "What is __name__?",
      "sidebar_tag": "__name__",
      "description": [
        "<p>Print the built-in variable <code>__name__</code>, with no",
        "modification.</p>",
        "<pre>&gt; python program.py",
        "__main__</pre>",
        "<p>Every Python file has a variable called <code>__name__</code>",
        "that Python fills in automatically. When a file is run",
        "<strong>directly</strong> (like every exercise on this site), its",
        "value is exactly the string <code>\"__main__\"</code>.</p>",
        "<p>That value changes, though, if this same file were instead",
        "<em>imported</em> into another Python file &mdash; in that case,",
        "<code>__name__</code> would hold the file's actual module name",
        "instead. That difference is what the rest of this unit is",
        "about.</p>"
      ],
      "starter": [
        "# TODO: print __name__"
      ],
      "tests": [
        {
          "stdin": [],
          "expected": "__main__"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "02",
      "source_unit": "main-guard",
      "title": "A Basic Guard",
      "sidebar_tag": "if __name__",
      "description": [
        "<p>Define a function <code>greet()</code> that prints",
        "<code>Hello!</code>. Instead of calling it directly, call it inside",
        "an <code>if __name__ == \"__main__\":</code> block.</p>",
        "<pre>&gt; python program.py",
        "Hello!</pre>",
        "<p>Since <code>__name__</code> equals <code>\"__main__\"</code>",
        "whenever a file is run directly, this <code>if</code> is true right",
        "now &mdash; but if another program imported this file to reuse",
        "<code>greet()</code>, that same <code>if</code> would be false,",
        "and <code>greet()</code> wouldn't run automatically just from being",
        "imported.</p>"
      ],
      "starter": [
        "def greet():",
        "    # TODO: print \"Hello!\"",
        "",
        "# TODO: call greet() inside an if __name__ == \"__main__\": block"
      ],
      "tests": [
        {
          "stdin": [],
          "expected": "Hello!"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "03",
      "source_unit": "main-guard",
      "title": "Moving Code into main()",
      "sidebar_tag": "def main()",
      "description": [
        "<p>Define a function <code>add(a, b)</code> that returns",
        "<code>a + b</code>. Then define a function <code>main()</code> that",
        "reads two integers, calls <code>add()</code>, and prints the",
        "result. Call <code>main()</code> inside an",
        "<code>if __name__ == \"__main__\":</code> block.</p>",
        "<pre>&gt; python program.py",
        "3",
        "4",
        "7</pre>",
        "<p>This is the standard shape of a Python script: helper functions",
        "defined first, a <code>main()</code> function that ties them",
        "together, and a guard at the very bottom that kicks everything",
        "off.</p>"
      ],
      "starter": [
        "def add(a, b):",
        "    # TODO: return a + b",
        "",
        "def main():",
        "    # TODO: read a and b, call add(a, b), and print the result",
        "",
        "# TODO: call main() inside an if __name__ == \"__main__\": block"
      ],
      "tests": [
        {
          "stdin": [
            "3",
            "4"
          ],
          "expected": "7"
        },
        {
          "stdin": [
            "10",
            "5"
          ],
          "expected": "15"
        },
        {
          "stdin": [
            "-2",
            "2"
          ],
          "expected": "0"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
